Regression guard added (`tests/test_document_stream_finalize_independent_write_js.py`, source-assertion style matching the repo's `*_js.py` convention): verified it fails on the old combined-guard code and passes on the fix; `node --check` clean on the edited file.

Fork-only (the block exists only on develop via the 67268d2b #4661 stopgap, not in upstream-mirror), so closed on landing to develop per the fork workflow.

For reproducibility — the observer instrumentation that captured the batched delivery (run in the page before `selectSession`, then drive `pinnedTopWalk` at ~30 ms cadence under ~40 ms emulated RTT and dump `window.__ioLog` at a stall):

```js
window.__ioLog = [];
const Native = window.IntersectionObserver;
let seq = 0;
window.IntersectionObserver = function (cb, opts) {
  const id = ++seq, log = window.__ioLog;
  const o = new Native(function (entries, obs) {
    log.push({t: performance.now()|0, id, ev: 'cb',
              inter: entries.map(e => e.isIntersecting)});
    return cb(entries, obs);
  }, opts);
  const obsFn = o.observe.bind(o), disFn = o.disconnect.bind(o);
  o.observe = (el) => { log.push({t: performance.now()|0, id, ev: 'observe', cls: el.className}); return obsFn(el); };
  o.disconnect = () => { log.push({t: performance.now()|0, id, ev: 'disconnect'}); return disFn(); };
  o.__id = id;
  return o;
};
```

Captured tail at the stall (observer 36 is the armed one; every earlier observer shows the healthy `[false]` then `[true]` two-delivery pattern — 36 got both in one delivery and died):

```
{id: 35, ev: 'cb', inter: [false]}
{id: 35, ev: 'cb', inter: [true]}
{id: 35, ev: 'disconnect'}      // healthy cycle: enter seen, batch loaded
{id: 36, ev: 'observe'}
{id: 36, ev: 'cb', inter: [false, true]}   // batched leave+enter — entries[0] read, enter discarded
// (nothing further; geometry check at the stall: sentinel bottom 70 vs zone edge cTop-300 → in zone)
```

The committed regression (`test_pinned_top_walk_completes`) encodes the same provoking shape without the shim.

